    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "A parabola has $x$-intercepts at $x=-1$ and $x=6$. The $y$-intercept is 12. Find the equation.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=-2(x+1)(x-6)$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=k(x+1)(x-6)\\\\12&=k(0+1)(0-6)\\\\k&=-2\\\\\\therefore y&=-2(x+1)(x-6)\\end{align*}$$",
